{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Abolish the Prayer Card System in the House of Commons",
        "additional_details": "The current prayer card system gives MPs who attend morning prayers preferential access to seats in the House of Commons. With only 427 seats available for 650 MPs, this creates an unfair advantage based on participation in religious observances. Parliament should uphold equality and religious freedom. Access to parliamentary seats should not depend on an MP\u2019s religious beliefs or willingness to participate in prayer. Abolishing this system would ensure fairer access for all MPs.",
        "background": "We ask the UK Parliament to abolish the prayer card system in the House of Commons, ending the practice of allowing MPs who attend prayers to reserve their seats for the remainder of the parliamentary day.",
